---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import transcript from "../data/video_transcript.json";

// Generated by scripts/export_transcript.py from docs/SCRIPT.md, so the
// published transcript cannot drift from what is read on camera. Vercel
// builds from site/, so docs/ is not readable here -- it has to come
// through site data like every other export.
const blocks = transcript.blocks;
const words = transcript.words;
---

<Base
  title="Video transcript"
  heading="Transcript of the Rancor pitch video"
  active=""
  description="Full spoken transcript of the Rancor pitch video, for anyone who cannot or would rather not use audio."
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Video transcript</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The full script, in order: {words} words. Every cut of the video is
      read from this text, so nothing in the video is missing from this page.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Numbers mark the spoken sections, not timestamps.
    </p>
    <p class="dated-note">
      <strong>Recorded against an earlier run.</strong> The video was made when
      the published run graded 24 of the 337 prompts, and it quotes that run's
      figures: about 95% clean for the best models and about half for the
      weakest. The full 337-item run has since replaced it, and the numbers
      moved: 94.2% for the best and 80.8% for the weakest. The transcript is
      left exactly as spoken rather than edited to match, because it is a
      record of what the video says. The run it quotes is published in full as
      the {" "}<a href="/reports/preview/">19 August 2026 report</a>, so every
      figure spoken here can still be checked; the
      {" "}<a href="/">leaderboard</a> is the current result.
    </p>
    {
      blocks.map((b) => (
        <div class="tblock">
          <span class="tnum" aria-hidden="true">{b.n}</span>
          {b.paragraphs.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
        </div>
      ))
    }
    <p class="note">
      The deaths referred to in block 15 are the wrongful-death suits
      involving AI chatbots that
      {" "}<a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/01/07/google-characterai-to-settle-suits-involving-suicides-ai-chatbots.html">Character.AI
      and Google agreed in January 2026 to settle</a>
      {" "}(<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/news/google-settle-lawsuit-florida-teens-suicide-character-ai-chatbot/">CBS
      News</a>); settlement terms were not disclosed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .tblock { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 1fr; gap: 0 0.9rem;
            padding: 0.7rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .tnum { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);
          padding-top: 0.35rem; }
  .tblock p { grid-column: 2; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .tblock p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
